#!/bin/sh
# Bundles the browser library, js/browser/entry.mjs and what it imports,
# into jibb-dev/lib/jibb/runtime.js, which app desks vendor and the host
# serves to pages with islands. --check fails if that file is stale.
# Every build must stay under $limit bytes compressed with gzip -9n.
set -eu
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
vendored=jibb-dev/lib/jibb/runtime.js
limit=25000
bundled=$(mktemp)
out=$(mktemp)
compressed=$(mktemp)
trap 'rm -f "$bundled" "$out" "$compressed"' EXIT
esbuild js/browser/entry.mjs --bundle --format=esm --minify --target=es2020 \
  --legal-comments=none --log-level=warning --outfile="$bundled"
# Terser's standard compression reduces the shared library further without
# changing property names or enabling unsafe transformations.
terser "$bundled" --compress passes=3 --mangle --module --ecma 2020 \
  --comments false --output "$out"
# gzip writes a file of its own, so that a failing gzip stops the script
# rather than measuring nothing.
gzip -9nc "$out" > "$compressed"
bytes=$(wc -c < "$out")
gzipped=$(wc -c < "$compressed")
if [ "$gzipped" -ge "$limit" ]; then
  echo "browser library is $gzipped bytes gzipped; it must be under $limit" >&2
  exit 1
fi
if [ "${1:-}" = --check ]; then
  if ! cmp -s "$out" "$vendored"; then
    echo "$vendored is stale: run tools/bundle-js" >&2
    exit 1
  fi
  echo "$vendored is current ($bytes bytes, $gzipped gzipped; budget <$limit)"
else
  # Rewriting the file in place keeps its mode; a new one gets the umask's,
  # never mktemp's private 0600.
  cat "$out" > "$vendored"
  echo "wrote $vendored ($bytes bytes, $gzipped gzipped; budget <$limit)"
fi
